  "summary": "Missing dot-stuffing after a bare LF or CR allows SMTP command injection",
  "details": "Someone who controls the content of a message with bare LF or CR line endings\ncan end it early with `\\n.\\n` on a server that takes a bare LF for a line\nending. What follows is read by the server as SMTP commands, which can be used\nto send other messages over the same authenticated connection.\n\nThis affects messages passed to `send_raw`, and message bodies that are sent\nwithout being encoded. The LF line endings of a `String` body are converted to\nCRLF before it is sent.",
